[h1]Phobos Medical 0.1.1[/h1]
[b]Draft - not published | 2026-10-04[/b]

[h2]Changed[/h2]

[list]
[*]The Ward-3 now has its own Halewright artwork: a 2075 sickbay bed with capped treatment cartridges at its head, two folded treatment arms, side treatment plates, a segmented cushion and a maintenance drawer at its foot. It replaces the vanilla medical bed's art on every form; a damaged bed shows the game's damage tint. The cartridges and arms are fictional nanomedical styling only: the bed's care is unchanged, the game's own medical-rest healing.
[*]The art was generated by OpenAI's built-in image tool from an original text prompt, chosen by the owner, and fitted to the 3 x 5 footprint by a recorded mechanical step. An earlier hospital-bed design and its separate fitting were set aside for this one.
[/list]

[h2]Compatibility and limits[/h2]

[list]
[*]Automatic. Saved beds show the new art when the save loads; nothing saved changes.
[*]Requires Phobos Framework 0.82.0 or newer. Offline checks are not gameplay validation; how the art looks in the game, lit and rotated, is still to be checked.
[/list]
